# oracle_license.rules
#
# Format:
#   SEVERITY|SOURCE|LITERAL_PATTERN
#
# SEVERITY: WARNING or CRITICAL
# SOURCE:   OPTION, FEATURE, PARAM, COMPONENT, META, SIGNAL, or ANY
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - OPTION means capability reported TRUE by V$OPTION. This does NOT prove use.
# - FEATURE means historical usage reported by DBA_FEATURE_USAGE_STATISTICS.
# - SIGNAL is additional technical evidence collected by this project.
# - PARAM includes parameters such as control_management_pack_access.
# - Rules must reflect YOUR Oracle contracts and the licensing rules for the
#   exact Oracle Database release being checked.
#
# Nothing is active by default to avoid false compliance assertions.

# Examples only - uncomment/adapt when the feature is not licensed:
# CRITICAL|FEATURE|Partitioning
# CRITICAL|FEATURE|Advanced Compression
# CRITICAL|FEATURE|Database Vault
# CRITICAL|FEATURE|Real Application Testing
# CRITICAL|FEATURE|SQL Tuning Advisor
# CRITICAL|SIGNAL|ACTIVE_DATA_GUARD_LIKE|YES
# WARNING|OPTION|Partitioning
# WARNING|OPTION|Advanced Compression
# WARNING|PARAM|DIAGNOSTIC+TUNING
# WARNING|SIGNAL|RAC_CONFIGURED|TRUE
# WARNING|SIGNAL|TDE_ENCRYPTED_TABLESPACES|
